"Speed limits, connections per torrent, upload slots and seeding are set for each torrent when you add it, or later under Torrent Settings. Torrents use the proxy from the Connection tab (HTTP or SOCKS5, or the Mac's proxy with \"Use the system settings\") and the speed limit for all downloads. Changes apply to torrents started afterwards. Peers and trackers can see your IP address, or your proxy's." = "Ko ngā tepe tere, ngā hononga i ia torrent, ngā taupānga tāpiritanga me te tāruatanga e tautuhia ana mō ia torrent ina tāpiritia e koe, i muri rānei i raro i te Torrent Settings. Ka whakamahia e ngā Torrents te hoakōkī mai i te tīpae Whakapānga (HTTP, SOCKS5 rānei, te hoakōkī Mac rānei me te \"Ka whakamahia ngā whakaritenga pūnaha\") me te tepe tere mō ngā tāruatanga katoa. Ka hoatu ngā huringa ki ngā torrents i tīmata i muri mai. Ka kitea e ngā hoariri me ngā kaiārahi tō koe tuakiri IP, o tō koe rānei.";
"Settings used for every download from a website. A site also covers its subdomains (example.com covers www.example.com). Logins are only sent to that site and are kept with the app's other secrets." = "Ka whakamahia ngā whakaritenga mō ia whakataki mai i tētahi pūnaewele. Ka taupoki hoki tētahi pae i ōna rohe-roto (example.com e taupoki ana i te www.example.com). Ka tukuna anake ngā tāurunga ki taua pae, ā, ka pupuritia ki ētahi atu mōhiotanga o te taupānga.";
"A backup holds your settings, site settings, queues and the downloads list. Passwords and cookies are never put in a backup." = "Kei roto i tētahi uho tōtahi o kāu whakaritenga, ngā whakaritenga pae, ngā uho, me te rārangi whakahua. Kāore anō kia kōkuhua ngā kuputuhi me ngā kuki i roto i tētahi uho.";
"When you copy a link that ends in one of these types, the Add window opens with it." = "Ki te tārua e koe i tētahi pātahitanga e whakamutu ana i tētahi o ēnei momo, ka whakatuwheratia te matapihi o Te Tāpiri ki a ia.";
"Expected checksums are checked automatically when a download finishes. Queues can also quit the app, sleep or shut down the Mac when they are done (Scheduler)." = "Ka whakamātauria ā-māoritia ngā uara whakamātau i te mutunga o te whakataki. Ka taea hoki e ngā kōwae te wehe i te taupānga, te moe, te whakakore rānei i te Mac ina oti rātau (Te Kaupapa).";
"Save the extension folder, open the browser's extensions page, switch on Developer mode, choose Load unpacked and pick the folder." = "Ka tiaki i te pūrākau whakarohenga, ka whakatuwheratia te pātū whakarohenga o te kaiwhaiwāhi, ka huri i te āhua o te kaiwhakawhanake, ka kōwhiri i te Whakahauhau i te whakawhanake, ā, ka kōwhiri i te pūrākau.";
"Save the add-on file and drag it onto a Firefox window. Firefox installs add-ons that are signed; see the README for signing your copy." = "Ka tiakina te faila tāpiri, ka tukua ki tētahi matapihi o Firefox. Ka whakatautautia e Firefox ngā tāpiri kua whakahētia; tirohia te README mō te whakatū i tōna tārua.";
"Install the ndm command, then for example: ndm https://example.com/file.zip --queue Night" = "Ka whakatū te whakahau ndm, kātahi hei tauira: ndm https://example.com/file.zip --queue Night";
"Finding the qualities on offer…" = "Finding the qualities on offer…";
